meta {
  name: Get Product Subpath - Assets
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06/assets
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data: isArray
  res.body.data[0].content_type: isString
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-07 against "David's Dev Account".

  ## What it does
  `GET /products/{id}/assets` -- returns the product's assigned assets
  fully expanded (matches `AssetOutputDto`: `id`, `content_type`,
  `checksum`, `extension`, `file_size`, `file_type`, `filename`, `path`,
  `n_catalogs`, `n_products`, `status`, `created`, `modified`).

  ## Assets subpath spot-check (Phase 0, ahead of Phase 2a)
  Also spot-checked `GET /assets/{id}/{path}` directly against one of this
  product's real assets (id `6a38f5e1c3d65a5f868b18a5`, a read-only
  fixture -- not created by this test, no mutation performed):
  - `GET /assets/{id}` -- 200, matches `AssetOutputDto`.
  - `GET /assets/{id}/categories` -- 200, `[]` (this asset isn't in any
    asset category).
  - `GET /assets/{id}/attributes`, `/relationships`, `/products` -- all
    **400** (`ValueError`, not in the asset's raw field list -- assets
    have no attributes/relationships concept, and there's no reverse
    `assets/{id}/products` lookup subpath).

  Full Bruno coverage for assets (create/patch, and confirming whether
  `DELETE /assets/{id}` truly doesn't exist per the spec) is deferred to
  Phase 2a's own `09-Assets/` folder, per `TESTING_PLAN.md`.
}
